1. Download & Install Git in windows/Mac
2. Open Terminal 
  -git --version
3. Set your Email & username if not set 
 -run the git config --list command and look for the user.name and user. email fields in the output.
 -To set 
 -git config --global user.name " your username "
 -git config --global user.email " your emailid "
 -To check which email is set git config --global user.email
4. Suppose You want to change these
  -git config --global --edit
5. Create Folder Using Git 
  -cd c 
  -mkdir LetsLearnGit
  -cd LetsLearnGit
  -git init (Now this folder is become repository & git initialized)
 -Check what we have in this folder 
  -ls
  -ls -a
 * a .git will now visible 
6. Now Add some files create some project / Fill that Folder 
 -git status
7. Now track & Add 
  -git add <filename>
  -git status
Now it is tracked / Staging area me agyi file
8. Now Commit 
  -git commit -m " "
9. To view How many Commits till Now made 
  -git log
10. To view what is done in status 
  -git status 
11. Do some changes & add some files then add & commit that too 
  -git add . / -git add <filename>
  -git commit -m " "
12. Now if you want to go to First commit you did 
  -git checkout <hash code of that commit/branch name>
  -Enter
ex: commit bc6d354bb6deafbf07ddd20e5ff7171268c12816 <---------This is the hash code I am talking about 
Author: Karan Gupta <karangupta4517@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Dec 13 12:55:09 2024 +0530
13. After this above command you will notice the Changes done On that Commit will visible & Current things Erased.
14. If User wants to go the current Commit/Latest Commit then type 
   -git checkout master

 
